## What changed from v1

| Feature | How it works |
|---|---|
| **Name+time grouping** | After email groups are formed, remaining rows are clustered using union-find: same normalized name + timestamps within `NAME_WINDOW_MIN` minutes → merged. Transitive — if A↔B and B↔C are each within 10 min, all three merge. |
| **`MatchType` column** | `email`, `name-time`, or `none` (singleton, no match found). |
| **`RawValues` column** | Each source row's original cells joined with `\|`, prefixed with `Row N:`, one per line. Multi-row merges show multiple lines so you can compare side-by-side. |
| **Name normalization** | Strips periods and collapses whitespace, so `A. Rivera` and `A Rivera` match. |
| **Backfill includes email** | If the latest row in a name-time group has no email but an older one does, it's filled in and the `no-email` issue clears. |

