| Change | Detail |
|---|---|
| **`KEEP_FIRST` flag** | Controls sort direction in `mergeGroup`. When `true`, rows sort ascending so the earliest timestamp wins; when `false`, latest wins (same as before). Null timestamps sort to the back either way so a real date always wins over a missing one. |
| **`KeepReason` column** | `kept-latest`, `kept-earliest`, or `single-row`. Derived inside `mergeGroup` from `KEEP_FIRST` and whether the group had more than one row. |
| **Column order** | `KeepReason` sits between `MatchType` and `Status` so the merge-related columns are together. |

Everything else — `DRY_RUN`, `NAME_WINDOW_MIN`, `RawValues`, `MatchType`, backfill logic, union-find clustering — is unchanged.

